        "rationale": "Real and UNDER-rated. Verified at axon-os/runtime.rs:218-242: `let exec = source.contains(\"exec(\") || source.contains(\"spawn_proc\")`. `exec (\"touch\", &args)` with one space parses identically and scans false. The reason this is worse than HIGH: runtime.rs:251 documents in its own comment that fs/exec are collapsed into a single IO bucket at runtime and that 'finer fs-vs-exec distinctions are enforced ONLY by the static gate'. So for any job granted fs_read or fs_write, this substring scan is the SOLE control separating exec=\"none\" from arbitrary process spawn — a single-space bypass of the only exec gate. Same root cause is already rated CRITICAL in the product-surface section of the same review, so HIGH here is an internal inconsistency. Other confirmed holes in the same fn: effects behind a `mod` import are invisible (only the top-level file is read); env_var, sleep_ms/now_ms, chan_*, goal_run/goal_eval, sql_query all scan as pure.",
