        "original_severity": "high",
        "rationale": "Confirmed by code read (NOT reproduced — building axon-os was out of budget for this triage, so confidence is code-level rather than empirical; flagging that explicitly). axon-os/runtime.rs:132-190: `child.stdout.take()`/`child.stderr.take()` happen at lines 138-139 but the `read_to_string` drains are at lines 181-182, strictly AFTER the try_wait/sleep loop breaks. The inline comment at 181 ('drained so the child isn't blocked on a full pipe') is self-refuting — the drain cannot unblock a child the loop is still waiting on. Once the child exceeds the 64 KiB Linux pipe buffer it blocks in write() forever and the loop kills it at the wall-clock timeout. Consequence is twofold: any verbose job is converted into a FALSE containment denial (`Denied{axis:\"time\"}`) recorded in the audit chain, and the 30s default turns it into a 30s stall. HIGH is correct — correctness/availability plus audit corruption, not a capability bypass.",
