        "rationale": "Verified at axon-os/monitor.rs:96-99: the poll loop's first statement is `if self.stop.load(Ordering::Acquire) { return MonitorResult::CleanExit; }` — an unconditional early return with no final read of the ledger from `current_offset`. cli.rs sets stop the instant the job process returns, and the loop sleeps 100ms between polls, so entries written in the final window are never parsed: containment_violation=false, exit 0, no kill trip, with the violating entry sitting on disk. This is precisely the exfiltrate-then-exit pattern, and the 100ms window is attacker-timeable. Note this is currently MASKED by OSK-P4-H4 (the ledger is never written at all), so it only becomes observable once H4 lands — sequencing matters but severity does not drop, since after H4 this is the adversarial case the monitor exists for.",
