        "rationale": "Verified at axon-os/cli.rs:272-280: `let kill_file_path = if killable && monitor_effects.is_none()`. With both flags the R27 file `$out/$run_id.kill` is never created and AXON_KILL_FILE is overwritten at cli.rs:284-287 to point at `$out/$run_id.monitor.kill`. `cmd_kill` reconstructs `$store/$run_id.kill` by naming convention — a file nobody polls — writes it, prints the tripped banner and exits 0; `cmd_status` reads back that same orphan file and reports TRIPPED while the job runs to completion. The operator kill-switch is inert AND affirmatively lies, in exactly the monitored configuration where an operator is most likely to reach for it. HIGH is right.",
