        "id": "OSK-P4-H8",
        "verdict": "confirmed",
        "severity": "high",
        "original_severity": "high",
        "rationale": "Verified at axon-os/cli.rs:247-257: `let approval_path = job_path.with_extension(\"approval\"); if approval_path.exists() { ... verify_approval ... }`. Absent token means the run proceeds with no sign-off check and no warning — the gate is opt-in by the presence of the very artifact it is supposed to demand. Perverse incentive confirmed: removing the token yields an unapproved run (exit 0) while editing the program with the token present yields exit 8. Second, independent defect also confirmed: verify_approval re-derives SHA-256 over public inputs only, with no key, so anyone can mint a token for any program/grant with `approved_by` set to any name — it is tamper-evidence, not authorization. HIGH is right; the signing half overlaps the pass-7 security critical about approval not being bound to the artifact, but the root causes differ (presence-gating vs. binding) and both fixes are needed.",
