        "rationale": "Verified. `collect_responses` (axon-vm/src/quorum/io.rs:63-77) globs every `*.vote` file in the directory, parses each, and returns all of them with no filtering; `cmd_run` (main.rs:977-984) passes them straight to `check_quorum(&votes, required_n)`. `VoteResponse` (quorum/logic.rs:45-60) has fields voter_tcb, run_id, approved, reason, lineage_root — and NO signature field, confirmed by reading the struct. `run_id` exists but is compared to nothing, and `--quorum` accepts no run-id or prog_hash to compare against. So three YES files approved for a benign proposal remain in votes/ and silently approve a later `axon-vm run dangerous.ax --quorum 3`. voter_tcb and lineage_root are equally self-asserted, defeating the anti-sock-puppet cap at logic.rs:83 — the exact opposite of coalition.rs:9-11's stated invariant that membership is supervisor-set and never self-reported. Since `axon deploy --quorum-dir DIR` gates Risk>=Critical on this, directory write access is deployment approval.",
