        "id": "OSK-P7-C1",
        "verdict": "confirmed",
        "severity": "critical",
        "original_severity": "critical",
        "rationale": "Verified by direct read of crates/axon-attest/src/lib.rs:191-225. `verify_report` performs exactly three checks: `report.signature.is_empty()`, `measurement.digest != *expected_digest`, and `measurement.axtcb1 != expected_axtcb1`. The HMAC is never recomputed and `hw_root` is never read at all — the parameter list does not even accept an expected hw_root. So a one-byte signature verifies, a report signed with an attacker's key verifies, and a software stand-in falsely claiming `hw_root = \"sev-snp\"` verifies and admits a job via try_admit_job. The SOFTWARE_TPM_HW_ROOT caveat the CLI prints to stderr is unenforceable by any relying party. Compounding: the signing key at axon-vm/src/main.rs:670-678 is SHA256(fixed-string || process::id()) — ~22 bits from a public value, brute-forceable even if the HMAC were checked. The module header advertises a fail-closed chain; it is fail-closed only against accidental corruption. Critical is correct — this is the root of trust for R26/R31.",
        "files_touched": [
          "crates/axon-attest/src/lib.rs",
          "crates/axon-vm/src/main.rs",
          "crates/axon-attest/tests/"
        ],
        "effort": "large",
        "behavior_change": true,
        "fix_sketch": "(1) Recompute the HMAC inside `verify_report` against a key the VERIFIER holds, passed in as a parameter — not one derivable from the prover's PID. (2) Replace the PID-derived key at main.rs:670-678 with a persisted operator key (or real TPM/SEV key material); a 22-bit key is not a key. (3) Add an `expected_hw_root: &str` parameter to verify_report that must match, and reject `sev-snp` unless a real SEV-SNP cert chain verifies. (4) Until (1)-(3) land, rename the function to `content_digest_matches` so no caller can read it as attestation, and make AttestationReport refuse to serialize a hw_root the producing substrate cannot back. Tests: forged signature, wrong-key signature, and hw_root=sev-snp from the software TPM must all be Err.",
