        "verdict": "confirmed",
        "severity": "critical",
        "original_severity": "critical",
        "rationale": "Verified by direct read of axon-guest-kernel/src/mmds.rs:256-282. `json_array_effects` returns `EffectSet(0xFF)` — ALL eight effects granted — when the key is absent (`None => return EffectSet(0xFF)`) and when the value is not an array (`if rest.is_empty() || rest[0] != b'[' { return EffectSet(0xFF) }`). The same open default is documented at lines 53-55, 106-108, 159-165, 184-187 for boot_params==0, missing axon.policy=, and POLICY_READY==false, and the static default is 0xFF too. This is an unsound default in the enforcement point of a security boundary — the exact deflation case the brief warns against, and here it is already correctly rated. The aggravating fact is that the reviewer's `allowed_effects: null` case is the DEFAULT axon-vm run emits for any program without an .axmeta manifest and no --principal, so the shipped default path grants IO+FS+Net+AI+Exec+Random. Also confirmed non-structural: `find_subslice` over raw bytes, first match wins, so duplicate keys diverge from any real JSON parser on the producer side.",
