      {
        "id": "OSK-P7-H1",
        "verdict": "confirmed",
        "severity": "high",
        "original_severity": "high",
        "rationale": "Verified at axon-vm/src/main.rs:1063: `\"ok\": result.is_ok()` where `result` is the LAUNCHER's Result (did we drive the Firecracker API), and exit_code is Firecracker's own process exit code — the guest program's status is never propagated. Firecracker exits 0 on KVM_EXIT_SHUTDOWN, so a guest triple fault is indistinguishable from success. I independently confirmed the reviewer's sub-claim (a): `grep -rn VIOLATION crates/axon-vm/src/` returns ZERO hits, so the `-VIOLATION8` serial sentinel that enforce.rs:253 writes with the comment 'so axon-vm can detect the exit code' has no parser anywhere — the advertised exit-8 SandboxViolation code is produced by nothing. A capability violation surfaces to the caller as ok:true. HIGH is right: it is a reporting/attestation-integrity failure on top of an enforcement that did fire.",
