      {
        "id": "OSK-P7-H2",
        "verdict": "confirmed",
        "severity": "high",
        "original_severity": "high",
        "rationale": "Verified. main.rs:2211-2279 (`measure_and_attest_inner`) compares SHA-256 of the kernel against `$HOME/.axon/kernel_baseline.sha256` (path constructed at 2224) and, when that file is absent, WRITES the current digest and returns Ok — textbook trust-on-first-use against a plain user-writable file with no integrity protection, so any attacker who can swap the kernel can `rm` the baseline. main.rs:2243 confirms the second bypass: `if env::var(\"AXON_CI_NO_KVM\").map(|v| v == \"1\")` short-circuits the gate entirely — an ordinary inherited environment variable, not a flag, disabling the boot gate on a production host. None of sign_report/verify_report/axtcb1 participate in this path. governance/REQUIREMENTS.md:72 states R26 as 'mandatory kernel attestation before every boot', which is false in two ways. HIGH is right. Note the fix's value is capped until OSK-P7-C1 lands, since verify_report itself checks no signature.",
