      {
        "id": "OSK-P7-H3",
        "verdict": "confirmed",
        "severity": "high",
        "original_severity": "high",
        "rationale": "Verified at axon-vm/src/chain.rs:268-287 (`verify_entries`). The loop checks only that each `entry.prev_hash` equals the running `prev` and that `compute_entry_hash(...)` reproduces `entry.entry_hash`. `entry.seq` is read only to name a failing entry in the Err return — never checked for contiguity — and the function returns `Ok(0)` immediately for an empty slice, so a fully erased chain verifies clean. A hash chain alone catches modification in place; it cannot catch truncation or wholesale deletion unless the tip is externally pinned, and nothing pins it (`--genesis` pins the ROOT, not the head, which is why the reviewer's four attacks all returned exit 0). Both chain.rs:5-7 and main.rs:150-154 assert that 'removing / substituting / reordering any run is detectable by chain verify'; removing is not. The auditor-facing export path (verify_export, which delegates to the same verify_entries) signs off on the rewritten chain too.",
        "files_touched": [
