        "effort": "medium",
        "behavior_change": true,
        "fix_sketch": "Two steps. Cheap and immediate: enforce `entry.seq == i` for all i inside `verify_entries` (returning Err(i) on a gap), so the log's own sequence numbers expose deletions and reordering, and make an empty chain verify only against an expected head of the genesis rather than unconditional Ok(0). Proper: have `verify` take an EXPECTED HEAD as well as an expected genesis (`--expected-head`), anchored outside the file — an operator-held or TPM-NV-backed tip, or a monotonic counter. Correct the two overclaiming doc strings at chain.rs:5-7 and main.rs:150-154 in the same change. Tests: delete the tip, delete all entries, and erase-and-restamp a middle entry — all three must fail verify.",
