        "severity": "high",
        "original_severity": "high",
        "rationale": "Same root cause as OSK-P4-H10: VoteResponse (quorum/logic.rs:45-60) carries no signature field and check_quorum treats voter_tcb and lineage_root as voter-supplied data, so any writer of the quorum directory can mint a passing quorum. I confirmed the struct definition directly. Keeping OSK-P4-H10 as the primary because its fix sketch is strictly broader — it covers BOTH the missing signature (this finding's angle) and the missing run_id/prog_hash binding that permits replaying an old approval onto a new program, and it names the vsock TCP-loopback peer-auth gap. One caveat for the scheduler: this finding carries one item NOT in OSK-P4-H10 — `default_coalition_cap` = ceil(N/2)-1 evaluates to 0 for N=1 and N=2, making quorum unsatisfiable for small fleets (REQUIREMENTS.md records verification only at N=3/4/6). That sub-item is already tracked as a separate MEDIUM ('Coalition cap makes quorum unsatisfiable for fleets of size 1 or 2') and is out of this batch's CRITICAL/HIGH scope, so nothing is lost by folding this finding.",
