        "verdict": "confirmed",
        "severity": "high",
        "original_severity": "high",
        "rationale": "Verified, and this is NOT the deferred-scope test-coverage pattern the brief warns about. I read scripts/gate.sh: it invokes exactly two scripts, vision_focus.sh (line 56) and parity_all.sh (line 130), and parity_all.sh globs `scripts/*_parity.sh` only. `grep -rln kernel_enforce_test .` returns only documentation files, the review itself, and the script — no automated caller. The surface left unwatched (R26 attestation, R31 extended TCB, R33 quorum, R34 chain, the guest syscall gate) is claimed '✅ Landed' in REQUIREMENTS.md, so this is unverified SHIPPED functionality, not deferred scope — and this batch confirmed four criticals and six highs sitting inside exactly that unwatched surface, which is the causal evidence that the gap matters. The reviewer's secondary point also holds: the four harnesses that do have a cargo-test caller treat SKIP as PASS, and both QEMU scripts prefer target/debug/axon, which the CLAUDE.md-documented fast build (--no-default-features) produces WITHOUT codegen, silently converting them to SKIP. Partially overlaps the repo-wide CI critical recorded elsewhere in this review, but this is the kernel-specific slice with a distinct deliverable.",
