        "id": "OSK-M01",
        "verdict": "confirmed",
        "severity": "medium",
        "original_severity": "medium",
        "behavior_change": true,
        "effort": "small",
        "files_touched": [
          "crates/axon-vm/src/main.rs"
        ],
        "rationale": "VERIFIED at crates/axon-vm/src/main.rs:882-899. The doc comment says the env var 'tightens the policy beyond the manifest' but the `if let Ok(forced) = env::var(\"AXON_VM_ALLOWED_EFFECTS\")` branch REPLACES the whole `allowed_effects` value — the manifest's `effect_union` and the principal's `allowed_effects` are only consulted in the `else` arm, so a forced set is never intersected with anything. Independently corroborated: governance/specs/R36-full-asi-os.md:137 and its S0 slice already record this exact defect ('must be checked as a subset rather than a replacement') as outstanding, so it is neither already-fixed nor a misread. Not raised above medium: the actor who sets the env var is the same actor who invokes `axon-vm run` and already controls the manifest and --principal flags, so this is a defense-in-depth/documentation-contradiction failure rather than a privilege crossing — but it is a real fail-open in the one place the guest syscall gate gets its policy, so not lowered either. Not reproduced by booting a VM (needs KVM/Firecracker); the control flow is unambiguous by inspection and I did not attempt a boot.",
        "fix_sketch": "In cmd_run (main.rs ~886), compute `base = manifest.effect_union.clone().or_else(|| principal.map(|p| p.allowed_effects.clone()))`. If AXON_VM_ALLOWED_EFFECTS is set, parse it into `forced`; if `base` is Some and `forced` is not a subset of `base`, eprintln the offending effects and exit 2; otherwise set allowed_effects = intersection(base, forced). If `base` is None (no manifest union, no principal), still refuse rather than honoring `forced` outright, so the env var can only narrow a policy that was derived from a signed source. Fix alongside OSK-M02 so the null/absent case is not silently re-opened downstream.",
        "conflicts_with": [],
