          "crates/axon-vm/src/main.rs",
          "scripts/axon_kernel_gate.sh",
          "scripts/r26_acceptance_gate.sh"
        ],
        "rationale": "VERIFIED every cited site in crates/axon-guest-kernel/src/mmds.rs: `static mut ALLOWED_EFFECTS: EffectSet = EffectSet(0xFF); // open by default` (line 41); `boot_params_phys == 0` -> set_open_policy (53-56); `cmdline_phys == 0` -> set_open_policy (66-69); `axon.policy=` absent -> set_open_policy (105-108); `read_policy()` returns EffectSet(0xFF) when !POLICY_READY (159-165); and `json_array_effects` returns `EffectSet(0xFF)` both when the key is missing and when the value's first non-ws byte is not `[` (262, 265). The reviewer's key claim that this fires on the ORDINARY path is sound by construction: with no --emit-manifest sidecar and no --principal, `allowed_effects` is None, serde emits `\"allowed_effects\":null`, `find_subslice` locates the key, `rest[0] == b'n'` != b'[' -> 0xFF. The 4095-byte truncation loop (77-84) is also as described (no null-terminator check). Corroborated as outstanding by governance/specs/R36-full-asi-os.md S0. Kept at medium rather than raised: the gate this policy feeds is itself advisory today (see OSK-M03 — ring 0, no interpreter ELF loaded), so an open policy currently authorizes nothing that a correct policy would have stopped. Kept at medium rather than lowered: it is a textbook unsound default in the component whose stated job is deny-by-default, it fires on the default run, and it becomes live the moment K5 lands. Not reproduced (requires a Firecracker/QEMU boot); verdict rests on reading every cited line.",
        "fix_sketch": "Invert all six defaults in mmds.rs to `EffectSet(0)`: change the ALLOWED_EFFECTS static initializer, make `set_open_policy()` into `refuse_boot(reason)` that kprintln!s and powers off with the violation exit code (8) on the boot_params/cmdline/tag-absent paths, return EffectSet(0) from read_policy() when !POLICY_READY, and return EffectSet(0) from json_array_effects on both the missing-key and non-`[` paths. In the cmdline copy loop (77-84) treat exhausting the 4095-byte buffer without seeing a NUL as a parse failure. Then fix the ordinary path in crates/axon-vm/src/main.rs so MmdsPayload.allowed_effects is never None — default to the explicit empty list (or refuse to launch without a derived policy) so `null` never reaches the guest. Update axon_kernel_gate.sh / r26_acceptance_gate.sh with a negative case asserting a policy-less boot now refuses instead of booting open.",
        "conflicts_with": [],
