        "effort": "large",
        "files_touched": [
          "crates/axon-guest-kernel/src/enforce.rs",
          "AXON_KERNEL.md",
          "governance/specs/R26-confidential-microvm-substrate.md"
        ],
        "rationale": "Every factual claim VERIFIED: `static mut ALLOWED_EFFECTS: u64 = 0xFF` at enforce.rs:31 with the comment conceding it matches the open mmds stub; `syscall_dispatch` (194-211) reads that writable static; `required_effect` (119-134) classifies syscalls 0 (read) and 1 (write) as `=> 0` i.e. 'Pure: always allowed regardless of policy' with no fd check; init() at ~425 says 'no real user mode here' for the STAR user-CS selector; run_program (295-323) states outright that the SYSRET path needs 'ring-3 user segments the boat GDT doesn't yet define' and that 'full interpreter ELF load + VFS is the remaining work'. So the finding is accurate. Severity lowered because there is no untrusted code inside the guest today — run_program is a hand-written demonstrator that issues one openat to prove the gate fires; the described attacker (a program that writes ALLOWED_EFFECTS or rewrites LSTAR) does not exist until the K5 interpreter load lands, and the source itself already documents the limitation at both cited sites. This is a deferred-scope architectural prerequisite, not a live defect, and per the calibration note I am not treating 'in a security-named module' as sufficient for medium. The only work shippable now is documentation honesty plus a recorded prerequisite; that is low. It must NOT be closed by documentation alone — flag it as a hard gate on the K5 slice.",
        "fix_sketch": "Two-part. Now (low cost, no behavior change): change the enforce.rs module doc and the K5 kprintln! strings from enforcement language to 'demonstration — the gate is advisory until ring-3 separation lands', and make the same correction in AXON_KERNEL.md and R26's description of the in-guest syscall gate. Add a `// PREREQUISITE FOR K5:` block at enforce.rs:31 listing the three requirements (user GDT descriptors + TSS, per-process page tables, policy page mapped read-only after init) and gate an fd-provenance check on syscalls 0/1 so they are not classified pure once a VFS exists. Later (large): land ring-3 separation as an explicit blocking item on the K5 interpreter-load slice, not as follow-up.",
