      {
        "id": "OSK-M05",
        "verdict": "confirmed",
        "severity": "medium",
        "original_severity": "medium",
        "behavior_change": true,
        "effort": "medium",
        "files_touched": [
          "crates/axon-vm/src/chain.rs",
          "crates/axon-vm/src/main.rs",
          "governance/specs/R34-incremental-attestation.md"
        ],
        "rationale": "VERIFIED at crates/axon-vm/src/chain.rs:98-116 — `compute_entry_hash` builds the preimage from VERSION_TAG ‖ prev_bytes ‖ prog_bytes ‖ run_id ‖ timestamp_ms.to_le_bytes() and `seq` is genuinely absent. VERIFIED at verify_entries (268-282) — the loop checks `entry.prev_hash != prev` and `recomputed != entry.entry_hash` and nothing else; there is no `entry.seq == index` assertion, so renumbering survives verification and `last_entry` then derives the next seq from the forged value. The truncation claim also holds: since verification is a pure forward walk from genesis, any prefix of a valid chain is itself a valid chain, and there is no persisted tip to compare against — `ChainExport.head` exists (line 260) but `verify` takes no expected head. This directly contradicts the module's own claim that removing any run is detected. Independently corroborated: R34's own 2026-07-31 adversarial fold-in row (spec line 1333) already records 'verify_entries checks only prev_hash linkage + recomputed entry_hash — no seq check, no SequenceGap'. Medium is right: exploiting it requires write access to chain.jsonl on the host, but detecting exactly that class of partial edit is the entire purpose of the chain, so the gap defeats the feature's stated contract. behavior_change true — adding seq to the preimage invalidates every existing chain file, hence the version bump.",
        "fix_sketch": "Add `preimage.extend_from_slice(&seq.to_le_bytes())` to compute_entry_hash (new `seq: u64` parameter) and bump VERSION_TAG to `axon-run-v2`; update both call sites (chain.rs append path and main.rs ChainCmd::Stamp). In verify_entries, track the index and return Err(entry.seq) when `entry.seq != index as u64`. For truncation, add a required `--head <axtcb1-run:…>` argument to `axon-vm chain verify` (and an `expected_head` parameter to verify_export) that must equal the last entry's entry_hash, so an out-of-band-anchored tip makes truncation detectable. Record the v1->v2 migration and the new --head requirement in R34 §4.2/§4.3.",
