      {
        "id": "OSK-M06",
        "verdict": "wrong-severity",
        "severity": "low",
        "original_severity": "medium",
        "behavior_change": true,
        "effort": "trivial",
        "files_touched": [
          "crates/axon-vm/src/quorum/logic.rs",
          "crates/axon-vm/src/main.rs"
        ],
        "rationale": "REPRODUCED. `default_coalition_cap` at quorum/logic.rs:83-85 is `required_n.div_ceil(2).saturating_sub(1)`; I compiled and ran the exact expression standalone: n=1 -> cap=0 (majority needed 1), n=2 -> cap=0 (needed 2), n=3 -> cap=1 (needed 2). The admission loop at 148-159 does `if *count >= cap { capped_out += 1; continue; }`, so with cap=0 the first YES of every lineage is rejected and `approvals` can never exceed 0, making `quorum_met = approvals > required_n/2` permanently false. I also confirmed there is no guard: crates/axon-vm/src/main.rs:969-984 passes `required_n` straight to check_quorum with only a --quorum-dir presence check, so `--quorum 1` and `--quorum 2` are permanent denies and the blocking_reason misattributes it to the coalition cap. Real bug. Downgraded to low because it fails CLOSED (a deny, never a spurious approve), and because n=1/n=2 are degenerate configurations where a per-lineage coalition ceiling is semantically meaningless — the correct fix is arguably a usage error rather than a permissive clamp. Impact is a confusing failure mode on two nonsensical settings, not a safety gap.",
        "fix_sketch": "Preferred: reject `--quorum < 3` in cmd_run (main.rs ~969) with a usage error explaining that a coalition ceiling requires at least 3 voters, before collect_responses runs. Alternatively clamp in logic.rs: `required_n.div_ceil(2).saturating_sub(1).max(1)`. Whichever is chosen, also fix the blocking_reason so a cap-driven deny at small N names the configuration rather than blaming the votes, and extend the parameterised coalition test to n = 1..12 (existing tests only cover n >= 3).",
        "conflicts_with": [],
        "blocks": [],
        "batch": "os-kernel-b"
      },
      {
        "id": "OSK-M07",
        "verdict": "confirmed",
