      {
        "id": "OSK-M08",
        "verdict": "confirmed",
        "severity": "medium",
        "original_severity": "medium",
        "behavior_change": true,
        "effort": "small",
        "files_touched": [
          "crates/axon-os/src/runtime.rs",
          "crates/axon-os/src/gate.rs"
        ],
        "rationale": "VERIFIED. crates/axon-os/src/runtime.rs:240 returns `max_label: Label::Internal` unconditionally for every successfully-read program — the surrounding scan derives fs_read/fs_write/net/exec from source substrings but the label is a hard-coded constant. crates/axon-os/src/gate.rs:67-75 denies when `declared.max_label > grant.max_label`, and grant.rs:38-42 orders `Public = 0, Internal = 1, Secret = 2` with a derived Ord, so Internal > Public and a `max_label = \"public\"` grant denies literally every program, including a trivially pure one. The tightest confidentiality ceiling in the model is therefore unreachable. Medium is correct: it is fail-closed (denies, never over-permits) so it is not a containment hole, but it makes an entire grant tier dead and pressures operators to grant `internal` for pure jobs, which is over-granting trained by the tool — a real security-hygiene defect, not merely cosmetic. Not reproduced end-to-end (would need an axon-os run with a public-grant manifest); the three cited code paths are unambiguous and mutually confirming. NOTE for scheduling: this file is also touched by OSK-M09 and OSK-M11.",
        "fix_sketch": "In runtime.rs scan_effects, derive the label instead of hard-coding it: default to `Label::Public`, raise to `Label::Internal` when the source mentions `@[sensitive]` or reads from a path outside the grant's public region, and reserve `Label::Secret` for `unknown()`'s read-failure path (which must stay maximally restrictive). Keep the derivation in the same closed-vocabulary style as the existing effect scan so it is auditable. Add two tests in gate.rs or runtime.rs: a pure program ADMITS under a `max_label = \"public\"` grant, and an `@[sensitive]`-annotated program is still DENIED under it.",
        "conflicts_with": [],
