        ],
        "rationale": "VERIFIED at crates/axon-attest/src/lib.rs:191-225. `verify_report` performs exactly three checks: `report.signature.is_empty()`, `report.measurement.digest != *expected_digest`, and `report.measurement.axtcb1 != expected_axtcb1`. The HMAC key is never re-derived and `report.hw_root` is never read anywhere in the function, so a report serialized with `hw_root: \"sev-snp\"` verifies identically to the software stand-in — a relying party has no way to require hardware. Low is the right severity and the finding itself is well-calibrated: the module doc-comment at 185-190 is explicitly honest ('the HMAC key is not re-checked here... Only real hardware provides cryptographic binding beyond operator control'), so this is a missing API affordance in a component that already advertises itself as a stand-in, not a misrepresentation. Blast radius is small: the only non-test caller is crates/axon-vm/src/main.rs:730 (cmd_attest), so adding a parameter is cheap. behavior_change true because a new required argument changes the verification outcome for software reports once hardware is demanded.",
        "fix_sketch": "Add a `require_hardware: bool` (or `expected_hw_root: Option<&str>`) parameter to verify_report; when set, reject `SOFTWARE_TPM_HW_ROOT` with a clear 'software stand-in report presented where a hardware root was required' error, and reject any hw_root not matching the expectation. Where an HMAC key is available, recompute and compare it so a garbage-but-non-empty signature is distinguishable from a valid one — the current `is_empty()` test only catches an absent signature. Update the single caller at crates/axon-vm/src/main.rs:730 to pass the operator's requirement (default false to preserve today's CI behavior, with a `--require-hw-attest` flag to turn it on).",
