        "rationale": "VERIFIED at crates/axon-os/src/cli.rs:543-546: the `\"--latest\" => { /* comment */ i += 1; }` arm advances the argument index and does nothing else — the flag is parsed and discarded. Confirmed the reviewer's second point too: the most-recent-.kill search it advertises is the fallback at 565-583 that runs only when `run_id.is_none()`, so `axon-os status <run-id> --latest` silently uses the explicit run-id and ignores the flag rather than overriding it. The flag is advertised to users in three places (USAGE at line 30, the help() string at 136, and the doc-comment at 531), so this is a genuine CLI-surface/behavior mismatch, not merely dead code. Low is correct — it is a read-only status command with no safety consequence.",
        "fix_sketch": "Honor the flag: add `let mut latest = false;` alongside the other parse locals, set it in the `\"--latest\"` arm, and change the kill_path selection at 565 from `if let Some(rid) = &run_id` to `if let (Some(rid), false) = (&run_id, latest)` so an explicit --latest forces the newest-.kill search even when a run-id is supplied. Keep the run_id_str fallback at the bottom (which already derives the id from the file stem) so the JSON output still names the run it actually read. If honoring it is not wanted, delete the arm and remove --latest from all three advertised strings (lines 30, 136, 531) instead — but do not leave it parsed-and-ignored.",
