        "fix_sketch": "Make the ceiling monotone. (1) interp.rs:477 — change `active_sandbox: Cell<i64>` to `active_sandboxes: RefCell<Vec<i64>>` (a stack); update the ctor at interp.rs:1818. (2) interp/builtins.rs:189-207 — replace the single `sbs.get(sb_handle)` lookup with a loop over EVERY frame on the stack, refusing if any frame's `allowed` set lacks the effect (intersection semantics). (3) interp/builtins.rs:2798 sandbox_create — if the stack is non-empty, intersect the requested effect set with the current effective ceiling before pushing the SandboxEntry (narrow-only), so a minted sandbox can never be wider than its creator's. (4) interp/builtins.rs:2819 sandbox_run — push/pop the handle instead of replace/set; keep both builtins exempt from the gate (that is now safe once the ceiling can only narrow). (5) Add a fail-first regression in crates/axon-core/tests/cli_run.rs asserting the nested-escape program above exits 8 (SandboxViolation) rather than 0.",
