        "rationale": "Same root cause as F134 [HIGH] in this batch: the R28 audit hook exists only in the interpreter's call_builtin and has no axon-rt/codegen counterpart, so native binaries silently ignore AXON_AUDIT_LEDGER. I verified the greps both findings rest on: `grep -rn 'axon_audit\\|axon-audit' crates/axon-rt/ crates/axon-ai/` returns zero hits, AXON_AUDIT_LEDGER appears only in axon-core/src/main.rs, axon-core/src/interp/builtins.rs and axon-web/src/api.rs, and AXON_AI_REPLAY appears only under axon-core (interp/provenance.rs, interp/builtins.rs, main.rs, tests/cli_run.rs). Keep F134 — it has the sharper evidence (a side-by-side 3-entries-vs-0 reproduction plus the reason the R28 acceptance gate structurally cannot reach the native path) and the better fix sketch (mirror the append in axon-rt + an audit_ledger_parity.sh). TWO residues of F074 are NOT covered by F134 and must be carried into its scope or they will be lost: (1) AXON_AI_REPLAY is likewise interp-only, so the F2 'byte-identical AI replay' guarantee silently does not hold for native artifacts; (2) the native agent-action store is a second, unchained log whose failures are all swallowed — which is F010's fail-open defect duplicated on the native side.",
