        "rationale": "Independently reproduced the exact measurement rather than trusting it: extracting every `name:` from the BUILTINS slice and word-matching against the concatenated README.md + spec/language-tour.md + spec/stdlib.md + spec/runtime.md + CLAUDE.md gives 290 distinct builtins, 187 mentioned nowhere — the finding's 294/188 to within the de-duplication difference. Spot-checked that the missing surface is the everyday library (dict_*, arr_map/filter/fold, str_split/join, as_i64/as_f64, bit ops) and that those builtins genuinely work. I am deliberately NOT applying the documentation-drift downgrade this repo's passes usually warrant: the usual pattern is a stale prose claim rated high, whereas this is 64% of the working public API having no reference at all, it is quantified, and the fix is mechanical (the BUILTINS table already carries name/params/ret/doc). Medium is correct — it is a learnability/product defect, not a correctness or security one, and it changes no behaviour.",
