        "rationale": "Every factual claim verified. `grep 'name: \"regex' crates/axon-core/src/builtins.rs` = 0 hits; the entire date/time surface is now_ms, sleep_ms, temporal_now/new/at/confidence/is_valid — no parsing, formatting, arithmetic or timezone anything. And the HTTP claim reproduced on the binary built by the documented command: `http_get(\"https://example.com\", \"\")` returns `ERR: http_get requires the asi-runtime feature or a network-capable host` and the program exits 0. The finding is real, well-scoped and honestly framed as a capability inventory rather than a bug. Severity left at medium: it is a feature-gap for a public release, and nothing is broken or unsound today.",
