        "id": "F183",
        "verdict": "confirmed",
        "original_severity": "medium",
        "severity": "medium",
        "rationale": "Confirmed by tracing the actual path. `Value::Struct { name: String, fields: HashMap<String, Value> }` at interp.rs:57-61; the FieldAccess arm (interp/eval.rs:403-408) evaluates the receiver and then `fields.get(field).cloned()`; and for an Ident receiver the Ident arm (interp/eval.rs:56-59) is `env.get(name).clone()` — a full deep clone of the map table plus every key String plus the struct's `name`, to read one field. So the ~6 allocations per single-field read on a 4-field struct follows directly from the code; I did not re-run the malloc counter, so the specific per-iteration figures are unverified by me. Not marked duplicate of F177 despite the shared root cause: F177 is the Index arm and F183 is the FieldAccess arm — different code, and the Vec+Rc field-name-table half of this fix has no analogue there. They MUST be scheduled together or serialized, since both edit crates/axon-core/src/interp/eval.rs and crates/axon-core/src/interp.rs.",
