        "rationale": "Both halves confirmed in code. `builtin_effect_row_agrees_with_impurity` (builtins.rs:2654-2680) iterates BUILTINS and asserts only `!row.is_empty() == impure` — a builtin absent from BOTH tables satisfies it trivially (false == false), which is exactly why the host_await family (F002/F059) passes it; I checked and found principal_activate and the whole kernel_goal_* family sitting in the same silent-pure state, so the omission class is broader than the one example. The handle tables are as described at interp.rs:448-475 (supervisors/stores/llm_gateways/goals/sandboxes are all append-only Vec with no release path). This is NOT the 'no test covers deferred-scope X' pattern the calibration note warns about — it is a test that provably fails to catch a confirmed HIGH finding, so it is a real gap. Low is correct: the test half enables other fixes rather than fixing anything itself, and the memory half is per-run monotonic growth in a short-lived process, which the finding itself offers 'document as intended' for.",
