        "id": "F060",
        "verdict": "confirmed",
        "severity": "high",
        "rationale": "Confirmed by code inspection, which is conclusive here. codegen/mod.rs:1187-1190 sets `self.current_agent_fn` only while emitting the @[agent] fn's OWN body (saved/taken per-fn at :1184), and asi.rs:35-37 early-returns when it is None. A helper fn is a separate emission with current_agent_fn = None, so any capability builtin one call-hop away emits no audit record. The interpreter is explicitly dynamic — interp.rs:1916-1921 reads `enclosing_agent` off the call stack with the comment 'the audit can't be escaped by indirection' — and interp/builtins.rs:172-179 is a single choke point. axon-rt has no agent context. This is exactly the transitive-laundering class the repo has already fixed three times elsewhere (R6 taint, @[contained], import-edge walk), never ported to native, in the one audit the docs call un-opt-out-able (I-13). I did NOT run the native empirical repro (the sandbox denied the cd-form command), so confidence rests on code reading — but the lexical/dynamic asymmetry is unambiguous in the source.",
