        "rationale": "All three technical sub-claims verified. (1) `grep sql_query crates/axon-core/src/builtins.rs` returns exactly one hit (:276) and it returns str — there is no database sink in the language. (2) `grep -rn sql_query crates/axon-core/src/codegen/` returns ZERO hits, and I reproduced the E0910 refusal building the demo's own safe exemplar list_records.ax, so the mechanism cannot appear in any compiled artifact. (3) collect_sql_injection (checker.rs:2579-2590) matches only a Call whose callee is the literal Ident `sql_query` with a non-literal first arg — it guards one builtin, not a property, so unsafe SQL strings remain freely representable. README.md:37 and WRITEUP.md:3/54/58 all carry '~28 of 40'. NEEDS-HUMAN because the fix is a product/marketing decision, not an engineering one: either restate the public headline number (a claim about the product) or commit to building a bound-parameter DB sink with codegen support. An agent should not silently rewrite the flagship pitch number.",
