        "rationale": "VERIFIED IN CODE. scripts/gdt_layout_ir_test.sh:79 is `BAD_STORES=\"$(grep -E 'store i64 [^,]+, ptr %(limit_lo|base_lo|base_mid|access|flags|base_hi)' \"$IR\" || true)\"` guarding an `if [[ -n \"$BAD_STORES\" ]]` fail. It is purely negative: an empty match passes, and the match is keyed to LLVM-named allocas that a codegen change, an SSA numbering change, or a field rename in examples/kernel/hello_kernel_slice3.ax would silently empty. There is no positive counterpart asserting N correct-width stores exist. I did not re-run the --emit-llvm probe (requires the codegen build); the reviewer's grep count of 12 is consistent with a 6-field GdtEntry. This is the same shape-vs-content class as the @[packed] i64-store bug the check was written to catch (see [[golden-ir-shape-vs-content-gap]]), so it earns a fix — but LOW is right: the check is live today, this is fragility not a present hole.",
