        "id": "DOC-01",
        "verdict": "confirmed",
        "severity": "critical",
        "original_severity": "critical",
        "rationale": "REPRODUCED. Rebuilt the codegen binary, ran `cd /tmp && axon build examples/hello.ax` -> ~100 `undefined reference to __axon_*` and `collect2: error: ld returned 1 exit status`. Same binary from the repo root succeeds in ~950ms. Code confirms the cause at link.rs:664: `std::env::var(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")` is read at RUNTIME (a cargo compile-time-only var, so always absent) and falls back to the relative `\"Cargo.toml\"`; the cargo subprocess has stdout/stderr piped to Stdio::null() and `if !status.success() { return None }` swallows it, after which link() proceeds without libaxon_rt.a. The documented headline native-AOT path is broken for every user who is not cd'd into the source checkout, and the failure has no diagnosis. Critical is correct — this is not doc drift, it is a shipped command that does not work.",
        "files_touched": [
          "crates/axon-core/src/codegen/link.rs"
        ],
        "effort": "medium",
        "fix_sketch": "In build_crate_staticlib (link.rs:655-720): replace `std::env::var(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")` with a compile-time `env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")` baked at build time, plus a runtime fallback that walks up from `std::env::current_exe()` to the first dir containing `Cargo.toml`; apply the same to the target-dir resolution at :714. Stop discarding subprocess output: capture stdout/stderr with Stdio::piped(), and on failure return an Err carrying cargo's stderr so link() at :332 aborts with `could not build/locate libaxon_rt.a: <stderr>` instead of silently linking a runtime-less object. Add a CLI integration test that runs `axon build` with cwd set to a temp dir. (Shipping a prebuilt libaxon_rt.a next to the binary is the longer-term fix and should be a separate task — it removes the cargo/source-tree runtime dependency.)",
