        "id": "RT-06",
        "verdict": "confirmed",
        "severity": "low",
        "original_severity": "low",
        "rationale": "Verified: __axon_ai_complete (crates/axon-ai/src/lib.rs:~248-265) calls `std::slice::from_raw_parts(prompt_ptr, prompt_len as usize)` behind only a 'Safety: the Axon codegen always passes valid str{ptr,len} pairs' comment, with no null/negative guard, while __axon_ai_extract_uncertain_i64 (:783) and its four siblings all start with `if prompt_ptr.is_null() || prompt_len < 0 { write_typed_err(...); return 1 }`. A negative len becomes a ~2^64 slice length (immediate UB). Unreachable via today's codegen contract, so low is exactly right — this is defense-in-depth consistency, not a live bug.",
