        "rationale": "Verified both halves. crates/axon-rt/src/provenance.rs record_with_input (~:107-121) unconditionally pushes a Record into a process-global Vec with no cap or eviction, and best_input_for scans it linearly. crates/axon-rt/src/lib.rs __axon_select (:192-215) is a `loop { for i in 0..count { ... } thread::sleep(Duration::from_micros(100)) }` round-robin poll whose own doc comment concedes 'a production runtime would use platform futexes', and the readiness it returns is advisory (another consumer can drain the channel before the arm recvs, and the arm then blocks). Both are honestly documented v1 simplifications, exactly the deferred-scope category the review is biased to over-report — low is the right call, and I would not raise it.",
